{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"release critique","packet_sha256":"076c05560cffdcc735568d17fa4a4c49af3fff3f1adaff306a1a92b7a51e6f94","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"a8c34855b3045feaa9128ac50f7297d29b450eb1bc3026482846b0bbf1e2ea07","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"release-proof-does-not-cover-patch-head","severity":"blocking","summary":"The supplied full-quality receipt predates the reviewed patch head, so it cannot lock in the two 8.7.1 fixes.","evidence":["The packet target is 98431a41c0e0b977a4431fc62a46817237d2a9e5.","charness-artifacts/release/8.7.0-prepush-quality.json records verified_head c10b107b5412b5b3ab093e5c305c56409fa74f1a.","The supplied release observer and release narrative concern v8.7.0 at commit 1d51de8a661805505794be554b478f0ced510b46, not an 8.7.1 candidate containing this patch.","No execution receipt in the semantic payload demonstrates the focused tests or release gate against 98431a41c0e0b977a4431fc62a46817237d2a9e5."],"action":"Run the proportionate focused tests and the release-quality gate on the exact 8.7.1 candidate head, then bind fresh receipts to that head before approval."},{"id":"mutation-source-scan-can-crash-on-non-utf8-file","severity":"blocking","summary":"The expanded mutation-pool source scan does not tolerate UnicodeDecodeError, despite the same file documenting a known non-UTF-8 repository fixture.","evidence":["tests_referencing_paths reads every candidate test and mutation-pool module with read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") but catches only OSError.","UnicodeDecodeError is not an OSError, so one non-UTF-8 candidate aborts the mapper instead of being skipped.","_local_loader_ancestor_levels explicitly catches (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError) and documents native/repograph/fixtures/non_utf8.py as a known non-UTF-8 fixture.","The new _candidate_module_sources contract expands scanning to the mutation pool, but the supplied tests cover OSError reads only and do not exercise a non-UTF-8 candidate source."],"action":"Handle UnicodeDecodeError consistently when building source_text and add a wired regression test containing a non-UTF-8 candidate module to prove the recommendation/probe completes."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"Muse may receive multiple effective workspaces and remain rooted at .agents.","bin":"resolved","disposition":"The command builder emits exactly one --workspace using the lane worktree, records that workspace, and has both argument-level and end-to-end coverage."},{"concern":"Trusting the Muse worktree may weaken containment.","bin":"non-blocking","disposition":"The reviewed command retains Muse's OS sandbox and disables interactive approval; --trust-workspace controls rule loading/delegation and is intentional for the disposable lane."},{"concern":"Existing v8.7.0 publication evidence should count as proof for the patch release.","bin":"rejected","disposition":"It proves an earlier release surface, not behavior or quality of the later 8.7.1 patch head."}],"next_move":"Repair and test the mutation scanner's non-UTF-8 boundary, then produce exact-head focused and release-quality evidence for the 8.7.1 candidate and rerun the bounded critique.","non_claims":["This review does not infer execution success from test source, recorded status, hashes, or an earlier release receipt.","This review does not assess current workspace content outside the supplied identity-bound semantic payload.","The Muse workspace patch is not declared live-host proven; the supplied evidence is source and test coverage only."]}
